{"content":[{"c":["BEDAN"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["1. One of Israel’s deliverers, along with Gideon, Jephthah, and Samuel, during the time of the judges (",{"href":"?bref=1Sam.12.11","r":"1Sam.12.11","rawR":"1Sam.12.11","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Sam.12.11","value":"1Sam.12.11"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Sm 12:11"},", ",{"c":["kjv"],"sourceClass":"sc","t":"span"},"; ",{"c":["rsv"],"sourceClass":"sc","t":"span"}," mg). The name Bedan may be either a shortened form of Abdon (",{"href":"?bref=Judg.12.13","r":"Judg.12.13","rawR":"Judg.12.13","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Judg.12.13","value":"Judg.12.13"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jgs 12:13"},") or a scribal error for Barak (",{"href":"?bref=Judg.4.6","r":"Judg.4.6","rawR":"Judg.4.6","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Judg.4.6","value":"Judg.4.6"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jgs 4:6"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["2. Ulam’s son, a descendant of Manasseh (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.7.17","r":"1Chr.7.17","rawR":"1Chr.7.17","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.7.17","value":"1Chr.7.17"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 7:17"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Bedan","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"1 Sm 12:11","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Sam.12.11","rawQueryValue":"1Sam.12.11","sourceRefExact":"1Sam.12.11"},{"anchorText":"Jgs 12:13","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Judg.12.13","rawQueryValue":"Judg.12.13","sourceRefExact":"Judg.12.13"},{"anchorText":"Jgs 4:6","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Judg.4.6","rawQueryValue":"Judg.4.6","sourceRefExact":"Judg.4.6"},{"anchorText":"1 Chr 7:17","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.7.17","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.7.17","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.7.17"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"67c799